{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"value","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLKeyAccidentalV5valueAA18MXLAccidentalValueOvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/value"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/value","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLKeyAccidental","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLKeyAccidental","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The key-accidental type indicates the accidental to be displayed in a non-traditional key signature,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represented in the same manner as the accidental type without the formatting attributes.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental","title":"MXLKeyAccidental"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental/value":{"title":"value","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/value","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/value","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"title":"MXLAccidentalValue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}